#  ERA5 reanalysis (Copernicus CDS, reanalysis-era5-pressure-levels plus
#  reanalysis-era5-single-levels, GRIB as the CDS serves it), 0.25 degree.
#  Authored from the WPS Vtable.ECMWF rows for the ECMWF t128 parameter
#  table.  CDS ERA5 surface fields are GRIB1 level type 1 (2 m and 10 m
#  fields included, as WPS Vtable.ECMWF has them); soil is level type 112
#  with the layer bounds in cm (the 100-289 cm layer is coded 100-255
#  because a GRIB1 octet cannot carry 289).
#  Pressure-level height is published as geopotential: GEOPT is scratch and
#  the blank HGT selector declares the writer's GEOPT / 9.81 output.  Terrain
#  is the surface geopotential (SOILGEO scratch, SOILHGT declared output),
#  exactly as the IFS open-data table does.  Snow is sd in metres of water
#  equivalent (SNOW_EC, x1000 rule) with the published snow density.
#  2 m humidity is dewpoint; the ecmwf map-source rule derives RH.
#  Sea-ice area fraction (ci) and SST are published, unlike the IFS
#  open-data step-0 product.
